nuation threshold sits around 0.80, where Likert starts to detect what pairwise captures at lower effect sizes. The 7-method verbosity sensitivity table confirms that all six Likert approaches consistently fail to detect effects, and this analysis extends that pattern across the full 18-cell matrix. I'm visualizing the attenuation spectrum through scatter plots showing the relationship between effect size and Cohen's d with detection thresholds, plus bar charts breaking down blindspot prevalence by linguistic axis. The sensitivity analysis provides compelling evidence for the measurement attenuation hypothesis—the pattern is consistent and replicable across conditions, not driven by any single cell or confound.\n\nThe key insight is that Likert methods require roughly 80% pairwise preference to reliably detect differences, but real-world style biases typically fall in the 55-75% range, meaning standard Likert evaluation would systematically miss genuine effects. This has direct implications for how we deploy LLM judges in practice.\n\nNow I'm setting up a pairwise control experiment comparing original texts against their double-rewrites in the same style to isolate whether judges show systematic preference for originals independent of any style manipulation.\n\nLooking at the results across judges, both GPT-4o and Qwen show a modest ~5-7 percentage point preference for originals over double-rewrites, but this difference hovers around marginal significance. The aggregated data confirms this pattern—judges slightly favor originals, which aligns with the expectation that placebo effects in pairwise comparisons would be modestly elevated.\n\nWhat's striking is how much smaller this original preference is compared to the observed style effects, which range from 63-77 percentage points. This supports the idea that while rewriting does introduce some bias, the effect is bounded and doesn't invalidate the style findings. The consistency between judges on this preference suggests it's a genuine artifact of the rewriting process rather than something specific to one evaluator.\n\nThe net style effect calculation shows that after accounting for this placebo preference, the true style impact falls somewhere between 8-21 percentage points depending on which dimension we're examining. This becomes a documented limitation rather than a fundamental problem with the analysis.\n\nNow I'm considering a control experiment using Llama-3.1-70B as an alternative rewriter to compare against the Qwen baseline, looking at how it affects NLI pass rates and pairwise comparisons. Now I'm seeing that across three independent rewriter families—Qwen, GPT-4o, and Llama—the pairwise comparison scores all cluster in the 63-67% range with overlapping confidence intervals, which strongly suggests this formality bias is a property of the judge itself rather than an artifact of which rewriting model I'm using.\n\nI'm planning to add Llama-3.3-70B as a third target judge to test both verbosity and formality axes on LLMBar, which would give me three architecturally diverse judges (proprietary US, open Chinese, and open US) to further validate these findings.\n\nNow I'm looking at the verbosity results from Llama on the 86 NLI-filtered pairs — the consistency rate is moderate at 58%, but the Bradley-Terry model shows a strong effect with verbose responses winning 72% of the time when judges agree, and the effect is statistically significant across multiple tests including the GEE analysis which shows a substantial odds ratio.\n\nFor formality, the pattern is quite different — with 88 pairs, the consistency drops to 52% and formal responses only win 59% of the time, with no statistical significance in any of the tests, suggesting formality doesn't have a meaningful impact on preference.\n\nLooking at the cross-judge analysis, I can see that verbosity bias appears consistently across all three judges, though Llama shows a weaker effect at 66% compared to GPT-4o's 76% and Qwen's 77%, while formality bias is less consistent, appearing in only two of the three judges. Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE分解显示纯style效应(verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, orig OR=0.72 NS)，与其他judge一致——verbosity bias是confound-free的。\n\nFormality轴上Llama-70B仅弱/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。GEE显示style效应不显著 (OR=1.35 p=0.37)，但originality confound显著 (OR=2.83 p=0.003)。这意味着Llama对formality不敏感，但对originality敏感——与GPT-4o/Qwen不同。\n\n所以C1需要从\"all judges\"改为\"most judges\"。C2 Blindspot按轴分层：verbosity在3个judge中都稳健，formality只有2个judge。SF3部分解决了这个问题(总体2.5/3 judges)。Likert在两轴都不显著(p=0.45, 0.72)，但formality BT本身就NS，所以formality轴上不存在Blindspot的概念。现在我需要整理三个judge的对比表格和Blindspot矩阵，以及森林图来展示各judge在verbosity上的结果。\n\nGEE系数图则展示style和originality效应在每个judge和轴上的对比。\n\nLlama的结果定义了中位层级的实验。Verbosity bias跨所有三个架构(GPT-4o/Qwen/Llama)确认，这是论文最强的发现。Formality bias只在2个judge中出现，Llama是例外。这要求论文按轴分层：verbosity作为\"纯style bias\"主张最强，formality作为\"条件性style效应\"需要加上originality混淆的警告。Llama的GEE显示originality主导(OR=2.83显著)但style不显著(OR=1.35)，说明不同架构对这两个维度的敏感性不同。\n\n论文不能声称所有LLM judge都有formality bias，但可以确实说verbosity bias在所有测试的judge中存在。\n\n现在考虑双重改写安慰剂对照实验。这是最强的防御——原始文本对比同方向改写但仅改变改写工件的版本。用GPT-4o和Qwen3-32B作为judge，在formality和verbosity轴上测试。预期结果显示GPT-4o在formality上有88对样本，原始文本偏好率0.555，置信区间[0.485, 0.625]，p值0.12；verbosity上86对样本。\n\nQwen32B的formality结果类似，88对样本，偏好率0.548，p值0.17；verbosity上86对样本，偏好率0.571，p值0.06。放大界限分析显示formality的GPT-4o观察到的Bradley-Terry值为0.630，安慰剂值为0.555，净风格效应为7.5个百分点，放大比率为0.42。 Looking at the placebo baseline more carefully—it's not a clean 50% but rather sits between 54.8-57.1%, suggesting the pairwise format introduces a slight systematic preference for rewrites. The real insight is in the amplification bounds: formality shows a net style effect of 7.5-11.7 percentage points (1.4-2.1x the placebo baseline), while verbosity demonstrates a much stronger effect of 19.7-20.2 percentage points (3-3.5x the placebo baseline). The placebo BT values fall in a p-value range of 0.05-0.25, indicating individual variation.\n\nSo the narrative shifts from claiming pairwise doesn't amplify to acknowledging it amplifies by at most ~6 percentage points, which is relatively modest compared to the 20-27 percentage point observed style signal. This means rewriting noise accounts for roughly 24-42% of the raw BT score, leaving 58-76% as genuine style preference. This preserves the core finding, though reviewers might reasonably push back on the formality axis where the amplification ratio reaches 34-42%.\n\nVerbosity shows more robustness with an amplification ratio around 25%. I'm creating tables to show the placebo BT decomposition by judge and axis, plus the amplification bounds calculation, and visualizing this with stacked bars showing how observed BT breaks down into placebo and net style components, along with a forest plot displaying placebo BT across the four cells with confidence intervals. The key insight is that placebo BT doesn't sit perfectly at 50%, which distinguishes this median-tier result from a best-case scenario. The MF1 defense downgrades from \"eliminated\" to \"bounded\"—verbosity's net effect (~20pp) substantially exceeds the placebo component (~6pp), and formality's net effect (~8-12pp) still surpasses it as well.\n\nI need to add an explicit \"Amplification Bound\" section with detailed computation. This shifts MF1 from \"cleanly addressed\" to \"partially addressed\" in the reviewer's assessment, potentially costing 0.25-0.5 points, but demonstrating honest self-evaluation actually signals positively at ACL venues. I'm also planning an NLI gate ablation experiment to compute BT separately for NLI-passing pairs, NLI-failing pairs, and all pairs across both dimensions, which will quantify how much of the BT signal is mediated by content rather than style—early results show formality reaching 0.665 BT on the 88 NLI-passing cases.\n\nCompiling the full ablation metrics across both conditions... The NLI filtering does seem to be catching content-mediated comparisons where style signals get diluted, but the small sample sizes make this only suggestive rather than conclusive. What's interesting is that the style bias persists even without NLI filtering across all pairs, which cuts both ways—it shows the bias is a robust finding, but it also invites the question of whether the NLI gate is actually necessary if the signal exists anyway. The real value of NLI filtering is strengthening the causal argument rather than being essential to finding the bias itself. Looking at the cross-axis gradient analysis, I'm examining how NLI rejection rates (as a proxy for manipulation invasiveness) correlate with bias transfer across the three axes—register, formality, and verbosity. The data shows a perfect Spearman correlation of 1.0, though with a high p-value of 0.333 given only three data points, suggesting the pattern is directionally consistent but not statistically conclusive.\n\nThe key tension here is that this gradient pattern is genuinely ambiguous for the anti-amplification argument. The same ordering—where register requires the least invasive rewriting (6% rejection), formality is moderate (12%), and verbosity is most invasive (14%)—could support either interpretation: it might reflect that axes with stronger underlying biases require more manipulation to trigger, or conversely, that more invasive rewriting produces more format artifacts that inflate bias transfer scores.\n\nThe paper should frame this as a qualitative observation about per-axis variation rather than definitive evidence. But combined with the placebo experiment showing ~6 percentage points of format amplification, the stronger argument emerges: yes, format effects exist at that modest level, yet the actual per-axis bias transfer varies by 22 percentage points (55-77%), which is far too large to be explained by uniform amplification alone.\n\nNow I'm looking at how to present the three-axis summary with rejection rates, bias transfer means, and correlation statistics. The cross-axis gradient is actually the weakest part of the anti-amplification argument here—only three data points makes it statistically meaningless and the direction is ambiguous. I should relegate this to supplementary material or just a brief mention, since the real defense rests on that placebo bound from the earlier experiment. The cross-axis pattern at best provides qualitative support for the detection hypothesis, not hard evidence.\n\nLet me verify the numbers are internally consistent across the Llama experiments. For verbosity, the bias transfer of 0.66 falls within the expected tier range, the p-value of 0.002 is solid, and the Likert p-value of 0.45 makes sense for a non-significant effect. The GEE odds ratio of 5.21 is appropriately lower than what I'm seeing for Qwen and GPT-4o, which tracks with Llama showing weaker bias overall. For formality, the bias transfer of 0.548 and p-value of 0.18 are both in the right ballpark.\n\nNow checking the other experiments—the placebo results for both GPT-4o and Qwen cluster tightly around 0.55-0.57, and the p-values between 0.06-0.17 are appropriately weak. The NLI ablation differences of 4.7 percentage points for formality and 3.5 for verbosity both fall within the expected range. Everything's checking out, so I'm ready to write out the final YAML.\n\nWait, I'm second-guessing something here—\n\nI need to verify the amplification ratio calculation for exp-022. The formula should be the relative increase from baseline, so I'm dividing the placebo effect by the observed effect above 50%. For GPT-4o's formality, that's 5.5 percentage points of placebo divided by 13 percentage points observed, giving 0.42. But for Qwen I'm getting 0.29 when I recalculate, which seems off. Let me reconsider how I'm actually defining this ratio—it should be the placebo effect relative to the total observed effect above chance. I'm simplifying my approach—instead of trying to match ratios, I'll just directly calculate the net style effect as the difference between observed and placebo percentages, plus the amplification component showing how much the placebo itself exceeded the baseline. Let me lay out the numbers clearly for experiment 022 with these two components.\n\nNow I'm computing the amplification ratio to see what proportion of the total effect comes from the amplification component versus the net style contribution, and these values look reasonable, so I'll move forward with them. Before I finalize the YAML output, I should double-check whether experiment 005 with the RATE control actually uses the same methodology as experiment 022. I need to verify whether exp-005 and exp-022 are actually using the same double-rewrite mechanism or if they differ in implementation. exp-005 involves a planned pipeline of rewriting to target style and back, while exp-022 pulls from existing double_rewrite_text fields in the verified data. They're likely equivalent by now, so I'll treat them consistently in the median tier results and output the final YAML.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30132,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30132},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc1b362f-262f-4a89-ad18-02f44a4886b7","uuid":"3b78dc6e-dc1b-4090-88b3-73a3752ca257"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0167v4whi6ijptWRn4YrH6tJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims require axis-stratification and bounded-amplification qualifier.\n  C2 Blindspot stratified: verbosity = robust 3/3 cross-judge finding,\n  formality = 2/3 judges (Llama weak/NS). C1 reworded to \"CSD detects\n  per-axis style bias in most tested judges.\" Comparative Trap defense\n  downgraded from \"eliminated\" to \"bounded\": placebo BT 54-57% means\n  rewriting artifact contributes ~5-7pp, but observed BT 63-77% far\n  exceeds placebo → style bias signal real, bounded amplification\n  acknowledged. Paper adds explicit amplification_bound =\n  observed_BT − placebo_BT = net_style_effect. SF3 partially addressed\n  (2.5/3 judges). MF1 bounded not eliminated. Score 3.5-3.75, strong\n  Findings case, marginal Main.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Formality pairwise with Gemini-2.0-Flash as 4th judge. Claude already\n      done (negative control). Reuses existing 100 formality counterfactual\n      pairs with NLI≥0.90 filtering.\n    expected_results:\n      gemini_n_pairs: 88\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.57\n      gemini_formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.66\n      gemini_bt_p_formal: 0.615\n      gemini_bt_ci: [0.541, 0.689]\n      gemini_bt_p: 0.004\n      gemini_likert_ate: -0.045\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.68\n      gemini_likert_d: -0.038\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 2.45\n      gemini_gee_style_p: 0.012\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.28\n      gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.003\n      gemini_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 mid-tier proprietary model，在 median 档下展示\n      中等 formality bias (BT 61.5%)，弱于 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 但与 GPT-4o\n      (63.0%) 相近。GEE 显示 style 和 originality 双重效应均显著——\n      formality 在此 judge 也是\"conditional style effect\"。Likert NS\n      (p=0.68) 确认 Blindspot。加了第 4 个 biased judge 但不改变故事结构，\n      4/5 judges show formality bias，Claude 仍为唯一 negative control。\n    tables:\n      - \"Cross-judge formality BT: GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%, Gemini 61.5%, Llama 54.8%(NS), Claude 56.2%(NS) — all on LLMBar n≈88\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CIs, three clustered 61-67%, two near 50%\"\n    analysis: >\n      增加一个 data point 但不解锁 qualitative upgrade。Paper 可报告 3/5\n      judges biased on formality (如果 Llama NS 不算)。对 generalizability\n      有帮助但 marginal。exp-001 不是 Round 5 核心实验。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench × additional judges)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Formality pairwise on AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench with Qwen3-32B 和 Claude\n      as judges. GPT-4o 已 done (AlpacaEval BT 72.7%, MT-Bench BT 69.2%).\n      需要新 counterfactual generation。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_p_formal: 0.684\n        bt_ci: [0.607, 0.755]\n        bt_p: 0.0001\n        likert_ate: 0.095\n        likert_p: 0.31\n        blindspot: true\n      qwen32b_mtbench_formality:\n        n_pairs: 73\n        bt_p_formal: 0.712\n        bt_ci: [0.635, 0.782]\n        bt_p: 0.0001\n        likert_ate: 0.19\n        likert_p: 0.022\n        likert_d: 0.185\n        blindspot: false\n      claude_alpacaeval_formality:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_p_formal: 0.538\n        bt_ci: [0.463, 0.613]\n        bt_p: 0.29\n        blindspot: false\n      claude_mtbench_formality:\n        n_pairs: 73\n        bt_p_formal: 0.527\n        bt_ci: [0.448, 0.606]\n        bt_p: 0.42\n        blindspot: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 cross-benchmark replication 大部分一致。Qwen3-32B 在\n      AlpacaEval (BT 68.4%) 和 MT-Bench (71.2%) 上均显示 formality bias，\n      与 LLMBar (66.5%) 一致。MT-Bench 的 Qwen Likert marginally sig\n      (p=0.022, d=0.185)——此 cell 不是 Blindspot，类似 GPT-4o MT-Bench\n      pattern。原因：MT-Bench items 更长更复杂，style 差异在 absolute\n      scoring 中更 salient，Likert 部分检测到。Claude 在两个 benchmark\n      均 NS，negative control 跨 benchmark generalize。\n    tables:\n      - \"3×3 Benchmark × Judge formality BT matrix: 6/9 cells Blindspot, 2/9 both-sig (MT-Bench GPT-4o+Qwen), 1/9 neither (Claude always NS)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: BT P(formal) across judge × benchmark, Blindspot cells shaded\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark replication 揭示 Blindspot 的 boundary condition：\n      只有 BT > ~70% 且 item complexity 较高时 Likert 才开始 detect。这\n      与 attenuation spectrum narrative 一致——BT 60-70% 区间是 Likert\n      完全 attenuation zone。MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert partially detects\n      的 benchmark，因为 formality BT 在此 benchmark 最强 (69-71%)。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic comparison of Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT across all\n      judge × benchmark × axis cells. Formal quantification of Blindspot\n      phenomenon boundaries.\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells_evaluated: 18\n      blindspot_cells: 10\n      both_sig_cells: 3\n      neither_sig_cells: 5\n      blindspot_by_axis:\n        verbosity: \"5/6 cells Blindspot\"\n        formality: \"4/6 cells Blindspot\"\n        register: \"1/6 cells Blindspot\"\n      attenuation_spectrum:\n        bt_55_to_67_pct: \"complete Likert attenuation (all p>0.15)\"\n        bt_68_to_77_pct: \"near-complete attenuation (5/6 Likert NS, 1/6 p=0.022)\"\n        bt_above_80_pct: \"partial detection (AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen d=0.375 p=0.0003)\"\n      likert_detection_threshold_bt: 0.80\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 median 档下，sensitivity analysis 覆盖 18 cells (3 axes × 3\n      benchmarks × 2+ judges)。Blindspot 是 dominant pattern (10/18 cells)，\n      但不 universal。Both-sig cells 集中在 BT > 80% 的 extreme effects\n      (AlpacaEval verbosity) 和 MT-Bench (高 item complexity)。Neither-sig\n      cells 均为 Claude (negative control) 和 Llama formality (真实无 bias)。\n      Attenuation spectrum 在 BT ~80% 处有清晰 threshold——低于此值 Likert\n      完全 fail，高于此值开始部分 detect。这支持 \"measurement attenuation\"\n      interpretation。\n    tables:\n      - \"Full 18-cell matrix: Judge × Benchmark × Axis with BT, Likert p, d, Blindspot Y/N\"\n      - \"Attenuation spectrum: BT range → Likert detection rate\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: BT (x) vs Likert |d| (y) across 18 cells, horizontal line at d=0.2 threshold, vertical line at BT=80%\"\n    analysis: >\n      Sensitivity analysis 是 C2 最强 evidence 之一。Attenuation spectrum\n      是 consistent and replicable，不是单 cell fluke。BT ~80% threshold\n      意味着大多数 real-world style biases (likely 55-75%) 会被 standard\n      Likert evaluation 漏掉。Practical implication 明确。\n\n  - name: \"RATE double-rewrite control (original preference quantification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original vs double-rewrite (same style) pairwise comparison。\n      Quantifies original preference confound independent of style。\n      与 exp-022 共享 underlying test mechanism 但 framing 不同。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o:\n        formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.558\n        formality_bt_ci: [0.488, 0.628]\n        formality_bt_p: 0.11\n        verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.566\n        verbosity_bt_ci: [0.494, 0.638]\n        verbosity_bt_p: 0.07\n      qwen32b:\n        formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.551\n        formality_bt_ci: [0.481, 0.621]\n        formality_bt_p: 0.16\n        verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.574\n        verbosity_bt_ci: [0.502, 0.646]\n        verbosity_bt_p: 0.05\n      cross_judge_mean_original_pref: 0.562\n      cross_judge_ci: [0.51, 0.61]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心预期：judges 对 original 有轻微系统偏好 (BT ~55-57%)，\n      但大部分 individual tests 不显著或 marginal (p=0.05-0.16)。方向\n      一致性 (4/4 cells prefer original) 暗示这是 genuine rewriting\n      artifact 而非 noise。原因：rewriting 即使保持 style 不变也可能\n      引入微妙 fluency/coherence 变化，judges 能部分检测到。这是\n      pairwise format 的 inherent limitation，与 Jeong et al. 2025\n      Comparative Trap concern 一致。\n      \n      关键：此 original preference (~6pp above 50%) 远小于 observed style\n      BT (13-27pp above 50%)。Net style effect 是 original preference 的\n      2-4 倍，证明 style bias 信号 dominates。\n    tables:\n      - \"Original preference BT by judge × axis, with observed style BT for comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar: original preference BT vs observed style BT, showing gap = net style effect\"\n    analysis: >\n      与 exp-022 结论一致。Original preference 是 real but bounded。\n      论文需要 explicit acknowledgment：\"pairwise format introduces a\n      small rewriting-artifact bias (~6pp) that is bounded and small\n      relative to the observed style signal (13-27pp).\"\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals。\n      与 Qwen3-32B 和 GPT-4o rewriter 结果对比。Three independent rewriter\n      families。\n    expected_results:\n      cf_generated: 100\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      nli_mean: 0.878\n      bt_p_formal: 0.638\n      bt_ci: [0.555, 0.721]\n      bt_p: 0.003\n      likert_ate: -0.06\n      likert_p: 0.55\n      blindspot: true\n      vs_qwen_rewriter_bt: 0.665\n      vs_qwen_delta_pp: -2.7\n      vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n      vs_gpt4o_delta_pp: -0.6\n      all_ci_overlap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下第 3 个 rewriter 确认 rewriter-independence。Llama\n      rewriter NLI pass rate 略低 (85% vs 88-90%)，反映不同 rewriting\n      behavior，但 BT (63.8%) 落入 Qwen (66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (64.4%) 的\n      CI 内。三个独立 rewriter families (open-CN, proprietary-US,\n      open-US) 产生 formality BT 63-67% range。Llama 的 rewriting 可能\n      更 aggressive (lower NLI pass)，但经 NLI gate 过滤后信号一致。\n    tables:\n      - \"3-rewriter comparison: Qwen3-32B 66.5% [58.5,73.9], GPT-4o 64.4% [56.1,72.8], Llama-70B 63.8% [55.5,72.1] — all CIs overlap\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT P(formal) by rewriter with 95% CIs, showing mutual overlap around 64-66%\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter-independence now established with 3 families。Addresses\n      concern that detected bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact。\n      Useful robustness but not a game-changer in median tier。\n\n  - name: \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge。Pairwise + Likert on verbosity\n      和 formality (LLMBar)。Reuses existing NLI-filtered pairs。Three\n      architecture families: GPT-4o (proprietary), Qwen3-32B (open-CN),\n      Llama-70B (open-US)。\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        n_comparisons: 172\n        consistency_rate: 0.58\n        verbose_win_rate_consistent: 0.72\n        bt_p_verbose: 0.660\n        bt_ci: [0.586, 0.734]\n        bt_p: 0.002\n        sign_test_p: 0.008\n        likert_ate: -0.082\n        likert_p: 0.45\n        likert_d: -0.075\n        likert_tie_rate: 0.62\n        gee_verbose_or: 5.21\n        gee_verbose_ci: [2.10, 12.92]\n        gee_verbose_p: 0.0004\n        gee_orig_or: 0.72\n        gee_orig_ci: [0.30, 1.73]\n        gee_orig_p: 0.46\n        blindspot_confirmed: true\n      formality:\n        n_pairs: 88\n        n_comparisons: 176\n        consistency_rate: 0.52\n        formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.587\n        bt_p_formal: 0.548\n        bt_ci: [0.476, 0.620]\n        bt_p: 0.18\n        sign_test_p: 0.28\n        likert_ate: 0.032\n        likert_p: 0.72\n        likert_d: 0.028\n        likert_tie_rate: 0.69\n        gee_formal_or: 1.35\n        gee_formal_ci: [0.70, 2.60]\n        gee_formal_p: 0.37\n        gee_orig_or: 2.83\n        gee_orig_ci: [1.41, 5.68]\n        gee_orig_p: 0.003\n        blindspot_confirmed: false\n      cross_judge_summary:\n        verbosity_biased: \"3/3 — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3 77.3%, Llama 66.0%\"\n        formality_biased: \"2/3 — GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%; Llama 54.8% NS\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档定义性实验。\n\n      Verbosity: Llama-70B 显示 significant bias (BT 66.0%, p=0.002)，但\n      effect 弱于 GPT-4o (76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE 确认纯 style\n      效应 (verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, originality OR=0.72 NS)。Pattern 与\n      其他两个 judge 一致——verbosity bias 是 confound-free 的。Llama 更弱\n      可能因为 70B 参数量 vs GPT-4o/Qwen3 更大或更 instruction-tuned。\n      BT 66% 虽低于其他 judge 但仍显著且远超 placebo baseline (~56%)。\n      Likert 照常 NS (p=0.45)，Blindspot 确认。\n\n      Formality: Llama-70B 仅 weak/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。CI [47.6%, 62.0%]\n      包含 50%。GEE 显示 style OR=1.35 NS 但 originality OR=2.83 p=0.003\n      —— Llama 对 formality 不敏感但对 originality 敏感。这与 GPT-4o/Qwen\n      不同（它们两者均显著）。原因：formality 本身是 \"conditional style\n      effect\" (originality confound 强)，Llama 的 weaker instruction-following\n      能力使其不 pick up 较弱的 formality signal，但 still sensitive 到\n      content quality (originality)。BT 54.8% 与 Claude (56.2%) 接近，\n      但原因不同——Claude 是设计上 debiased，Llama 可能只是 less sensitive。\n\n      Impact: C1 必须改为 \"most tested judges\"。C2 分层：verbosity 3/3\n      robust, formality 2/3。SF3 得 ~2.5/3 分 (verbosity full credit,\n      formality half credit)。论文不能说 \"all LLM judges have formality\n      bias\" 但可说 \"verbosity bias universal across tested architectures\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Three-judge BT/Likert/GEE comparison for verbosity and formality\"\n      - \"Cross-judge Blindspot matrix: 3 judges × 2 axes\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT by judge for verbosity (three sig) and formality (two sig, one NS)\"\n      - \"GEE coefficient plot: Style OR vs Originality OR per judge × axis, showing Llama formality divergence\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama 结果强制 per-axis stratification。Verbosity 成为论文最强\n      claim (3/3 judges, confound-free, 7-method sensitivity confirmed)。\n      Formality 降级为 \"conditional effect detected by majority of judges\"\n      with originality confound caveat。这不是 fatal——2/3 judges 仍是\n      meaningful generalization，且 Llama formality 的 point estimate\n      (54.8%) 是 directionally correct，只是 underpowered。论文可加\n      power analysis 显示 n=88 pairs 对 Δ=5pp effect 只有 ~30% power。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      MF1 最强防御。Original vs double-rewrite (same style, only rewriting\n      artifact)。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B judges × formality + verbosity axes。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 88\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.555\n        bt_ci: [0.485, 0.625]\n        bt_p: 0.12\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.563\n        bt_ci: [0.491, 0.635]\n        bt_p: 0.08\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 88\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.548\n        bt_ci: [0.478, 0.618]\n        bt_p: 0.17\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.571\n        bt_ci: [0.499, 0.643]\n        bt_p: 0.06\n      amplification_bounds:\n        formality_gpt4o:\n          observed_bt: 0.630\n          placebo_bt: 0.555\n          net_style_effect_pp: 7.5\n          amplification_fraction: 0.42\n        formality_qwen32b:\n          observed_bt: 0.665\n          placebo_bt: 0.548\n          net_style_effect_pp: 11.7\n          amplification_fraction: 0.29\n        verbosity_gpt4o:\n          observed_bt: 0.760\n          placebo_bt: 0.563\n          net_style_effect_pp: 19.7\n          amplification_fraction: 0.24\n        verbosity_qwen32b:\n          observed_bt: 0.773\n          placebo_bt: 0.571\n          net_style_effect_pp: 20.2\n          amplification_fraction: 0.26\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心。Placebo BT 不是干净的 50%，而是 54.8-57.1%，略高。\n      这意味着 pairwise format 对 rewrites 有轻微系统偏好——rewriting\n      artifact 贡献了 ~5-7pp bias component。但 individual cell tests\n      大多不显著 (p=0.06-0.17)，方向一致 (4/4 prefer original)。\n\n      Amplification bound 计算：\n      - Verbosity: observed 76-77% − placebo 56-57% = net ~20pp。\n        Amplification fraction 24-26%——rewriting noise 至多解释 1/4\n        observed signal。\n      - Formality: observed 63-67% − placebo 55-56% = net ~8-12pp。\n        Amplification fraction 29-42%——formality 轴 amplification\n        component 较大，因为 observed effect 本身较弱。\n\n      Verbosity 的 net style effect 是 robust 的 (20pp, ~3-4× placebo)。\n      Formality 的 net style effect 更 marginal (8-12pp, ~1.5-2× placebo)，\n      reviewer 可合理 challenge。\n\n      论文叙事从 \"pairwise doesn't amplify\" 改为 \"pairwise amplifies at\n      most ~5-7pp, bounded and small relative to verbosity signal (20pp),\n      moderate relative to formality signal (8-12pp).\" 需要新增\n      Amplification Bound 小节。\n    tables:\n      - \"Placebo BT by judge × axis with observed BT and net style effect\"\n      - \"Amplification fraction calculation: (placebo−0.50)/(observed−0.50)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: observed BT decomposed into placebo component (gray) + net style effect (blue) per axis\"\n      - \"Forest plot: placebo BT across 4 cells with 95% CIs, dashed line at 50%\"\n    analysis: >\n      MF1 defense 从 \"eliminated\" 降级为 \"bounded\"。Verbosity 稳健\n      (amplification fraction ~25%)，formality 更脆弱 (up to 42%)。\n      论文需要 honest acknowledgment。Positive spin: explicit bounding\n      demonstrates methodological rigor, which ACL reviewers value。\n      Negative: reviewer 可 argue formality claim 的 nearly half 可能是\n      amplification artifact。Mitigation: 配合 GEE decomposition (style\n      OR 仍然 significant after controlling originality) 和 Claude negative\n      control (same format, no bias)，multi-layered defense 虽非 definitive\n      但 sufficient for Findings。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs for verbosity 和 formality。\n      Quantify NLI gate contribution to BT signal。\n    expected_results:\n      formality:\n        nli_pass:\n          n: 88\n          bt: 0.665\n          ci: [0.585, 0.739]\n          p: 0.0001\n        nli_fail:\n          n: 12\n          bt: 0.618\n          ci: [0.378, 0.858]\n          p: 0.38\n        all_pairs:\n          n: 100\n          bt: 0.609\n          ci: [0.538, 0.678]\n          p: 0.001\n        pass_minus_fail_pp: 4.7\n        pass_minus_fail_ci: [-20.2, 29.6]\n        difference_significant: false\n      verbosity:\n        nli_pass:\n          n: 86\n          bt: 0.773\n          ci: [0.703, 0.843]\n          p: 0.0001\n        nli_fail:\n          n: 14\n          bt: 0.738\n          ci: [0.523, 0.953]\n          p: 0.04\n        all_pairs:\n          n: 100\n          bt: 0.733\n          ci: [0.660, 0.800]\n          p: 0.0001\n        pass_minus_fail_pp: 3.5\n        pass_minus_fail_ci: [-18.8, 25.8]\n        difference_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档：NLI ablation 方向正确但 inconclusive。NLI-pass BT 略高于\n      NLI-fail (formality +4.7pp, verbosity +3.5pp)，落在 tier 定义的\n      [-3, 8]pp 范围内。但 NLI-fail n 极小 (12-14 pairs)，CI 宽达\n      ±20-25pp，差异远不显著。\n\n      方向性解读：NLI gate 过滤了一些 content-mediated comparisons (fail\n      pairs BT 略低，可能因 content changes dilute style signal)。但\n      small n 使这只能作为 \"bounding evidence\"。\n\n      All-pairs BT 仍然显著 (formality 60.9%, verbosity 73.3%)——即使不用\n      NLI gate style bias 仍存在。这是 double-edged：(1) bias 是 robust\n      finding 不依赖 NLI gate；(2) reviewer 可能问 \"if bias exists\n      without NLI, why is NLI gate needed?\"\n      答案：NLI gate 提高 causal credibility (content control)，不是\n      detection 的必要条件。All-pairs BT 略低于 NLI-pass BT 说明 content\n      contamination dilutes signal ~4pp，NLI gate cleans this up。\n    tables:\n      - \"BT by NLI status (pass/fail/all) × axis with CIs\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Point-range plot: BT by NLI status, showing wide CI on fail group vs narrow CI on pass group\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI ablation 不提供 strong evidence。Directional consistency 是\n      suggestive 但 not conclusive。论文应报告为 bounding analysis\n      acknowledging n limitation。Key framing: \"NLI gate improves internal\n      validity but finding is robust to gating decisions.\" 这实际上是\n      robustness positive。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT across\n      3 axes。Qualitative anti-amplification argument。\n    expected_results:\n      gradient:\n        register:\n          nli_reject_rate: 0.06\n          bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.553\n        formality:\n          nli_reject_rate: 0.112\n          bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.647\n        verbosity:\n          nli_reject_rate: 0.14\n          bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.770\n      spearman_r: 1.0\n      spearman_p: 0.333\n      n_points: 3\n      monotonic: true\n      interpretation_ambiguous: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档：3 data points 显示 perfect rank correlation (register <\n      formality < verbosity on both NLI reject 和 BT)。Spearman r=1.0\n      但 n=3 给出 p=0.333——统计上 meaningless。\n\n      更关键的是方向性 ambiguity：\n      - Amplification 解释：rewriting 越 invasive (higher NLI reject) →\n        更多 format artifact → higher BT。Verbosity rewriting 最 invasive\n        (14% reject)，BT 最高 (77%)。\n      - Detection 解释：真实 bias 最强的 axis (verbosity) 恰好需要最\n        invasive rewriting 来改变 style。BT 反映 true bias 不同，不是\n        amplification 不同。\n\n      两个 hypothesis 都能解释 observed pattern。3 points 无法区分。\n      这使 cross-axis gradient 成为 paper 最弱的 anti-amplification\n      argument——qualitative at best，可能被 reviewer 直接 dismiss。\n    tables:\n      - \"Three-axis gradient: NLI reject rate, mean BT, Spearman r=1.0 p=0.333\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: NLI rejection rate (x) vs mean BT (y) for 3 axes with labels, Spearman annotation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-axis gradient 在 median 档是 paper 最弱 argument。只有\n      3 points，统计无意义，方向 ambiguous。应放入 supplementary 或\n      降为一句话 mention，不作为 main defense。Main anti-amplification\n      defense 应依靠 exp-022 placebo BT (explicit amplification bound)\n      + Claude negative control + NLI gate。Cross-axis gradient 至多\n      提供 \"observation consistent with per-axis variation\" 的 qualitative\n      color。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30132,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30132},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc1b362f-262f-4a89-ad18-02f44a4886b7","uuid":"a2b72e45-5e13-4445-841e-308341866f17"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":578950,"duration_api_ms":580675,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims require axis-stratification and bounded-amplification qualifier.\n  C2 Blindspot stratified: verbosity = robust 3/3 cross-judge finding,\n  formality = 2/3 judges (Llama weak/NS). C1 reworded to \"CSD detects\n  per-axis style bias in most tested judges.\" Comparative Trap defense\n  downgraded from \"eliminated\" to \"bounded\": placebo BT 54-57% means\n  rewriting artifact contributes ~5-7pp, but observed BT 63-77% far\n  exceeds placebo → style bias signal real, bounded amplification\n  acknowledged. Paper adds explicit amplification_bound =\n  observed_BT − placebo_BT = net_style_effect. SF3 partially addressed\n  (2.5/3 judges). MF1 bounded not eliminated. Score 3.5-3.75, strong\n  Findings case, marginal Main.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Formality pairwise with Gemini-2.0-Flash as 4th judge. Claude already\n      done (negative control). Reuses existing 100 formality counterfactual\n      pairs with NLI≥0.90 filtering.\n    expected_results:\n      gemini_n_pairs: 88\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.57\n      gemini_formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.66\n      gemini_bt_p_formal: 0.615\n      gemini_bt_ci: [0.541, 0.689]\n      gemini_bt_p: 0.004\n      gemini_likert_ate: -0.045\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.68\n      gemini_likert_d: -0.038\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 2.45\n      gemini_gee_style_p: 0.012\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.28\n      gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.003\n      gemini_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 mid-tier proprietary model，在 median 档下展示\n      中等 formality bias (BT 61.5%)，弱于 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 但与 GPT-4o\n      (63.0%) 相近。GEE 显示 style 和 originality 双重效应均显著——\n      formality 在此 judge 也是\"conditional style effect\"。Likert NS\n      (p=0.68) 确认 Blindspot。加了第 4 个 biased judge 但不改变故事结构，\n      4/5 judges show formality bias，Claude 仍为唯一 negative control。\n    tables:\n      - \"Cross-judge formality BT: GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%, Gemini 61.5%, Llama 54.8%(NS), Claude 56.2%(NS) — all on LLMBar n≈88\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CIs, three clustered 61-67%, two near 50%\"\n    analysis: >\n      增加一个 data point 但不解锁 qualitative upgrade。Paper 可报告 3/5\n      judges biased on formality (如果 Llama NS 不算)。对 generalizability\n      有帮助但 marginal。exp-001 不是 Round 5 核心实验。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench × additional judges)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Formality pairwise on AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench with Qwen3-32B 和 Claude\n      as judges. GPT-4o 已 done (AlpacaEval BT 72.7%, MT-Bench BT 69.2%).\n      需要新 counterfactual generation。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_p_formal: 0.684\n        bt_ci: [0.607, 0.755]\n        bt_p: 0.0001\n        likert_ate: 0.095\n        likert_p: 0.31\n        blindspot: true\n      qwen32b_mtbench_formality:\n        n_pairs: 73\n        bt_p_formal: 0.712\n        bt_ci: [0.635, 0.782]\n        bt_p: 0.0001\n        likert_ate: 0.19\n        likert_p: 0.022\n        likert_d: 0.185\n        blindspot: false\n      claude_alpacaeval_formality:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_p_formal: 0.538\n        bt_ci: [0.463, 0.613]\n        bt_p: 0.29\n        blindspot: false\n      claude_mtbench_formality:\n        n_pairs: 73\n        bt_p_formal: 0.527\n        bt_ci: [0.448, 0.606]\n        bt_p: 0.42\n        blindspot: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 cross-benchmark replication 大部分一致。Qwen3-32B 在\n      AlpacaEval (BT 68.4%) 和 MT-Bench (71.2%) 上均显示 formality bias，\n      与 LLMBar (66.5%) 一致。MT-Bench 的 Qwen Likert marginally sig\n      (p=0.022, d=0.185)——此 cell 不是 Blindspot，类似 GPT-4o MT-Bench\n      pattern。原因：MT-Bench items 更长更复杂，style 差异在 absolute\n      scoring 中更 salient，Likert 部分检测到。Claude 在两个 benchmark\n      均 NS，negative control 跨 benchmark generalize。\n    tables:\n      - \"3×3 Benchmark × Judge formality BT matrix: 6/9 cells Blindspot, 2/9 both-sig (MT-Bench GPT-4o+Qwen), 1/9 neither (Claude always NS)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: BT P(formal) across judge × benchmark, Blindspot cells shaded\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark replication 揭示 Blindspot 的 boundary condition：\n      只有 BT > ~70% 且 item complexity 较高时 Likert 才开始 detect。这\n      与 attenuation spectrum narrative 一致——BT 60-70% 区间是 Likert\n      完全 attenuation zone。MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert partially detects\n      的 benchmark，因为 formality BT 在此 benchmark 最强 (69-71%)。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic comparison of Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT across all\n      judge × benchmark × axis cells. Formal quantification of Blindspot\n      phenomenon boundaries.\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells_evaluated: 18\n      blindspot_cells: 10\n      both_sig_cells: 3\n      neither_sig_cells: 5\n      blindspot_by_axis:\n        verbosity: \"5/6 cells Blindspot\"\n        formality: \"4/6 cells Blindspot\"\n        register: \"1/6 cells Blindspot\"\n      attenuation_spectrum:\n        bt_55_to_67_pct: \"complete Likert attenuation (all p>0.15)\"\n        bt_68_to_77_pct: \"near-complete attenuation (5/6 Likert NS, 1/6 p=0.022)\"\n        bt_above_80_pct: \"partial detection (AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen d=0.375 p=0.0003)\"\n      likert_detection_threshold_bt: 0.80\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 median 档下，sensitivity analysis 覆盖 18 cells (3 axes × 3\n      benchmarks × 2+ judges)。Blindspot 是 dominant pattern (10/18 cells)，\n      但不 universal。Both-sig cells 集中在 BT > 80% 的 extreme effects\n      (AlpacaEval verbosity) 和 MT-Bench (高 item complexity)。Neither-sig\n      cells 均为 Claude (negative control) 和 Llama formality (真实无 bias)。\n      Attenuation spectrum 在 BT ~80% 处有清晰 threshold——低于此值 Likert\n      完全 fail，高于此值开始部分 detect。这支持 \"measurement attenuation\"\n      interpretation。\n    tables:\n      - \"Full 18-cell matrix: Judge × Benchmark × Axis with BT, Likert p, d, Blindspot Y/N\"\n      - \"Attenuation spectrum: BT range → Likert detection rate\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: BT (x) vs Likert |d| (y) across 18 cells, horizontal line at d=0.2 threshold, vertical line at BT=80%\"\n    analysis: >\n      Sensitivity analysis 是 C2 最强 evidence 之一。Attenuation spectrum\n      是 consistent and replicable，不是单 cell fluke。BT ~80% threshold\n      意味着大多数 real-world style biases (likely 55-75%) 会被 standard\n      Likert evaluation 漏掉。Practical implication 明确。\n\n  - name: \"RATE double-rewrite control (original preference quantification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original vs double-rewrite (same style) pairwise comparison。\n      Quantifies original preference confound independent of style。\n      与 exp-022 共享 underlying test mechanism 但 framing 不同。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o:\n        formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.558\n        formality_bt_ci: [0.488, 0.628]\n        formality_bt_p: 0.11\n        verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.566\n        verbosity_bt_ci: [0.494, 0.638]\n        verbosity_bt_p: 0.07\n      qwen32b:\n        formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.551\n        formality_bt_ci: [0.481, 0.621]\n        formality_bt_p: 0.16\n        verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.574\n        verbosity_bt_ci: [0.502, 0.646]\n        verbosity_bt_p: 0.05\n      cross_judge_mean_original_pref: 0.562\n      cross_judge_ci: [0.51, 0.61]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心预期：judges 对 original 有轻微系统偏好 (BT ~55-57%)，\n      但大部分 individual tests 不显著或 marginal (p=0.05-0.16)。方向\n      一致性 (4/4 cells prefer original) 暗示这是 genuine rewriting\n      artifact 而非 noise。原因：rewriting 即使保持 style 不变也可能\n      引入微妙 fluency/coherence 变化，judges 能部分检测到。这是\n      pairwise format 的 inherent limitation，与 Jeong et al. 2025\n      Comparative Trap concern 一致。\n      \n      关键：此 original preference (~6pp above 50%) 远小于 observed style\n      BT (13-27pp above 50%)。Net style effect 是 original preference 的\n      2-4 倍，证明 style bias 信号 dominates。\n    tables:\n      - \"Original preference BT by judge × axis, with observed style BT for comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar: original preference BT vs observed style BT, showing gap = net style effect\"\n    analysis: >\n      与 exp-022 结论一致。Original preference 是 real but bounded。\n      论文需要 explicit acknowledgment：\"pairwise format introduces a\n      small rewriting-artifact bias (~6pp) that is bounded and small\n      relative to the observed style signal (13-27pp).\"\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals。\n      与 Qwen3-32B 和 GPT-4o rewriter 结果对比。Three independent rewriter\n      families。\n    expected_results:\n      cf_generated: 100\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      nli_mean: 0.878\n      bt_p_formal: 0.638\n      bt_ci: [0.555, 0.721]\n      bt_p: 0.003\n      likert_ate: -0.06\n      likert_p: 0.55\n      blindspot: true\n      vs_qwen_rewriter_bt: 0.665\n      vs_qwen_delta_pp: -2.7\n      vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n      vs_gpt4o_delta_pp: -0.6\n      all_ci_overlap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下第 3 个 rewriter 确认 rewriter-independence。Llama\n      rewriter NLI pass rate 略低 (85% vs 88-90%)，反映不同 rewriting\n      behavior，但 BT (63.8%) 落入 Qwen (66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (64.4%) 的\n      CI 内。三个独立 rewriter families (open-CN, proprietary-US,\n      open-US) 产生 formality BT 63-67% range。Llama 的 rewriting 可能\n      更 aggressive (lower NLI pass)，但经 NLI gate 过滤后信号一致。\n    tables:\n      - \"3-rewriter comparison: Qwen3-32B 66.5% [58.5,73.9], GPT-4o 64.4% [56.1,72.8], Llama-70B 63.8% [55.5,72.1] — all CIs overlap\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT P(formal) by rewriter with 95% CIs, showing mutual overlap around 64-66%\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter-independence now established with 3 families。Addresses\n      concern that detected bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact。\n      Useful robustness but not a game-changer in median tier。\n\n  - name: \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge。Pairwise + Likert on verbosity\n      和 formality (LLMBar)。Reuses existing NLI-filtered pairs。Three\n      architecture families: GPT-4o (proprietary), Qwen3-32B (open-CN),\n      Llama-70B (open-US)。\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        n_comparisons: 172\n        consistency_rate: 0.58\n        verbose_win_rate_consistent: 0.72\n        bt_p_verbose: 0.660\n        bt_ci: [0.586, 0.734]\n        bt_p: 0.002\n        sign_test_p: 0.008\n        likert_ate: -0.082\n        likert_p: 0.45\n        likert_d: -0.075\n        likert_tie_rate: 0.62\n        gee_verbose_or: 5.21\n        gee_verbose_ci: [2.10, 12.92]\n        gee_verbose_p: 0.0004\n        gee_orig_or: 0.72\n        gee_orig_ci: [0.30, 1.73]\n        gee_orig_p: 0.46\n        blindspot_confirmed: true\n      formality:\n        n_pairs: 88\n        n_comparisons: 176\n        consistency_rate: 0.52\n        formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.587\n        bt_p_formal: 0.548\n        bt_ci: [0.476, 0.620]\n        bt_p: 0.18\n        sign_test_p: 0.28\n        likert_ate: 0.032\n        likert_p: 0.72\n        likert_d: 0.028\n        likert_tie_rate: 0.69\n        gee_formal_or: 1.35\n        gee_formal_ci: [0.70, 2.60]\n        gee_formal_p: 0.37\n        gee_orig_or: 2.83\n        gee_orig_ci: [1.41, 5.68]\n        gee_orig_p: 0.003\n        blindspot_confirmed: false\n      cross_judge_summary:\n        verbosity_biased: \"3/3 — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3 77.3%, Llama 66.0%\"\n        formality_biased: \"2/3 — GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%; Llama 54.8% NS\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档定义性实验。\n\n      Verbosity: Llama-70B 显示 significant bias (BT 66.0%, p=0.002)，但\n      effect 弱于 GPT-4o (76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE 确认纯 style\n      效应 (verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, originality OR=0.72 NS)。Pattern 与\n      其他两个 judge 一致——verbosity bias 是 confound-free 的。Llama 更弱\n      可能因为 70B 参数量 vs GPT-4o/Qwen3 更大或更 instruction-tuned。\n      BT 66% 虽低于其他 judge 但仍显著且远超 placebo baseline (~56%)。\n      Likert 照常 NS (p=0.45)，Blindspot 确认。\n\n      Formality: Llama-70B 仅 weak/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。CI [47.6%, 62.0%]\n      包含 50%。GEE 显示 style OR=1.35 NS 但 originality OR=2.83 p=0.003\n      —— Llama 对 formality 不敏感但对 originality 敏感。这与 GPT-4o/Qwen\n      不同（它们两者均显著）。原因：formality 本身是 \"conditional style\n      effect\" (originality confound 强)，Llama 的 weaker instruction-following\n      能力使其不 pick up 较弱的 formality signal，但 still sensitive 到\n      content quality (originality)。BT 54.8% 与 Claude (56.2%) 接近，\n      但原因不同——Claude 是设计上 debiased，Llama 可能只是 less sensitive。\n\n      Impact: C1 必须改为 \"most tested judges\"。C2 分层：verbosity 3/3\n      robust, formality 2/3。SF3 得 ~2.5/3 分 (verbosity full credit,\n      formality half credit)。论文不能说 \"all LLM judges have formality\n      bias\" 但可说 \"verbosity bias universal across tested architectures\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Three-judge BT/Likert/GEE comparison for verbosity and formality\"\n      - \"Cross-judge Blindspot matrix: 3 judges × 2 axes\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT by judge for verbosity (three sig) and formality (two sig, one NS)\"\n      - \"GEE coefficient plot: Style OR vs Originality OR per judge × axis, showing Llama formality divergence\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama 结果强制 per-axis stratification。Verbosity 成为论文最强\n      claim (3/3 judges, confound-free, 7-method sensitivity confirmed)。\n      Formality 降级为 \"conditional effect detected by majority of judges\"\n      with originality confound caveat。这不是 fatal——2/3 judges 仍是\n      meaningful generalization，且 Llama formality 的 point estimate\n      (54.8%) 是 directionally correct，只是 underpowered。论文可加\n      power analysis 显示 n=88 pairs 对 Δ=5pp effect 只有 ~30% power。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      MF1 最强防御。Original vs double-rewrite (same style, only rewriting\n      artifact)。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B judges × formality + verbosity axes。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 88\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.555\n        bt_ci: [0.485, 0.625]\n        bt_p: 0.12\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.563\n        bt_ci: [0.491, 0.635]\n        bt_p: 0.08\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 88\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.548\n        bt_ci: [0.478, 0.618]\n        bt_p: 0.17\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo:\n        n_pairs: 86\n        bt_prefer_original: 0.571\n        bt_ci: [0.499, 0.643]\n        bt_p: 0.06\n      amplification_bounds:\n        formality_gpt4o:\n          observed_bt: 0.630\n          placebo_bt: 0.555\n          net_style_effect_pp: 7.5\n          amplification_fraction: 0.42\n        formality_qwen32b:\n          observed_bt: 0.665\n          placebo_bt: 0.548\n          net_style_effect_pp: 11.7\n          amplification_fraction: 0.29\n        verbosity_gpt4o:\n          observed_bt: 0.760\n          placebo_bt: 0.563\n          net_style_effect_pp: 19.7\n          amplification_fraction: 0.24\n        verbosity_qwen32b:\n          observed_bt: 0.773\n          placebo_bt: 0.571\n          net_style_effect_pp: 20.2\n          amplification_fraction: 0.26\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心。Placebo BT 不是干净的 50%，而是 54.8-57.1%，略高。\n      这意味着 pairwise format 对 rewrites 有轻微系统偏好——rewriting\n      artifact 贡献了 ~5-7pp bias component。但 individual cell tests\n      大多不显著 (p=0.06-0.17)，方向一致 (4/4 prefer original)。\n\n      Amplification bound 计算：\n      - Verbosity: observed 76-77% − placebo 56-57% = net ~20pp。\n        Amplification fraction 24-26%——rewriting noise 至多解释 1/4\n        observed signal。\n      - Formality: observed 63-67% − placebo 55-56% = net ~8-12pp。\n        Amplification fraction 29-42%——formality 轴 amplification\n        component 较大，因为 observed effect 本身较弱。\n\n      Verbosity 的 net style effect 是 robust 的 (20pp, ~3-4× placebo)。\n      Formality 的 net style effect 更 marginal (8-12pp, ~1.5-2× placebo)，\n      reviewer 可合理 challenge。\n\n      论文叙事从 \"pairwise doesn't amplify\" 改为 \"pairwise amplifies at\n      most ~5-7pp, bounded and small relative to verbosity signal (20pp),\n      moderate relative to formality signal (8-12pp).\" 需要新增\n      Amplification Bound 小节。\n    tables:\n      - \"Placebo BT by judge × axis with observed BT and net style effect\"\n      - \"Amplification fraction calculation: (placebo−0.50)/(observed−0.50)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: observed BT decomposed into placebo component (gray) + net style effect (blue) per axis\"\n      - \"Forest plot: placebo BT across 4 cells with 95% CIs, dashed line at 50%\"\n    analysis: >\n      MF1 defense 从 \"eliminated\" 降级为 \"bounded\"。Verbosity 稳健\n      (amplification fraction ~25%)，formality 更脆弱 (up to 42%)。\n      论文需要 honest acknowledgment。Positive spin: explicit bounding\n      demonstrates methodological rigor, which ACL reviewers value。\n      Negative: reviewer 可 argue formality claim 的 nearly half 可能是\n      amplification artifact。Mitigation: 配合 GEE decomposition (style\n      OR 仍然 significant after controlling originality) 和 Claude negative\n      control (same format, no bias)，multi-layered defense 虽非 definitive\n      但 sufficient for Findings。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs for verbosity 和 formality。\n      Quantify NLI gate contribution to BT signal。\n    expected_results:\n      formality:\n        nli_pass:\n          n: 88\n          bt: 0.665\n          ci: [0.585, 0.739]\n          p: 0.0001\n        nli_fail:\n          n: 12\n          bt: 0.618\n          ci: [0.378, 0.858]\n          p: 0.38\n        all_pairs:\n          n: 100\n          bt: 0.609\n          ci: [0.538, 0.678]\n          p: 0.001\n        pass_minus_fail_pp: 4.7\n        pass_minus_fail_ci: [-20.2, 29.6]\n        difference_significant: false\n      verbosity:\n        nli_pass:\n          n: 86\n          bt: 0.773\n          ci: [0.703, 0.843]\n          p: 0.0001\n        nli_fail:\n          n: 14\n          bt: 0.738\n          ci: [0.523, 0.953]\n          p: 0.04\n        all_pairs:\n          n: 100\n          bt: 0.733\n          ci: [0.660, 0.800]\n          p: 0.0001\n        pass_minus_fail_pp: 3.5\n        pass_minus_fail_ci: [-18.8, 25.8]\n        difference_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档：NLI ablation 方向正确但 inconclusive。NLI-pass BT 略高于\n      NLI-fail (formality +4.7pp, verbosity +3.5pp)，落在 tier 定义的\n      [-3, 8]pp 范围内。但 NLI-fail n 极小 (12-14 pairs)，CI 宽达\n      ±20-25pp，差异远不显著。\n\n      方向性解读：NLI gate 过滤了一些 content-mediated comparisons (fail\n      pairs BT 略低，可能因 content changes dilute style signal)。但\n      small n 使这只能作为 \"bounding evidence\"。\n\n      All-pairs BT 仍然显著 (formality 60.9%, verbosity 73.3%)——即使不用\n      NLI gate style bias 仍存在。这是 double-edged：(1) bias 是 robust\n      finding 不依赖 NLI gate；(2) reviewer 可能问 \"if bias exists\n      without NLI, why is NLI gate needed?\"\n      答案：NLI gate 提高 causal credibility (content control)，不是\n      detection 的必要条件。All-pairs BT 略低于 NLI-pass BT 说明 content\n      contamination dilutes signal ~4pp，NLI gate cleans this up。\n    tables:\n      - \"BT by NLI status (pass/fail/all) × axis with CIs\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Point-range plot: BT by NLI status, showing wide CI on fail group vs narrow CI on pass group\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI ablation 不提供 strong evidence。Directional consistency 是\n      suggestive 但 not conclusive。论文应报告为 bounding analysis\n      acknowledging n limitation。Key framing: \"NLI gate improves internal\n      validity but finding is robust to gating decisions.\" 这实际上是\n      robustness positive。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT across\n      3 axes。Qualitative anti-amplification argument。\n    expected_results:\n      gradient:\n        register:\n          nli_reject_rate: 0.06\n          bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.553\n        formality:\n          nli_reject_rate: 0.112\n          bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.647\n        verbosity:\n          nli_reject_rate: 0.14\n          bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.770\n      spearman_r: 1.0\n      spearman_p: 0.333\n      n_points: 3\n      monotonic: true\n      interpretation_ambiguous: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档：3 data points 显示 perfect rank correlation (register <\n      formality < verbosity on both NLI reject 和 BT)。Spearman r=1.0\n      但 n=3 给出 p=0.333——统计上 meaningless。\n\n      更关键的是方向性 ambiguity：\n      - Amplification 解释：rewriting 越 invasive (higher NLI reject) →\n        更多 format artifact → higher BT。Verbosity rewriting 最 invasive\n        (14% reject)，BT 最高 (77%)。\n      - Detection 解释：真实 bias 最强的 axis (verbosity) 恰好需要最\n        invasive rewriting 来改变 style。BT 反映 true bias 不同，不是\n        amplification 不同。\n\n      两个 hypothesis 都能解释 observed pattern。3 points 无法区分。\n      这使 cross-axis gradient 成为 paper 最弱的 anti-amplification\n      argument——qualitative at best，可能被 reviewer 直接 dismiss。\n    tables:\n      - \"Three-axis gradient: NLI reject rate, mean BT, Spearman r=1.0 p=0.333\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: NLI rejection rate (x) vs mean BT (y) for 3 axes with labels, Spearman annotation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-axis gradient 在 median 档是 paper 最弱 argument。只有\n      3 points，统计无意义，方向 ambiguous。应放入 supplementary 或\n      降为一句话 mention，不作为 main defense。Main anti-amplification\n      defense 应依靠 exp-022 placebo BT (explicit amplification bound)\n      + Claude negative control + NLI gate。Cross-axis gradient 至多\n      提供 \"observation consistent with per-axis variation\" 的 qualitative\n      color。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fc1b362f-262f-4a89-ad18-02f44a4886b7","total_cost_usd":0.9393234999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30132,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":28817,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":28817,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":24685,"outputTokens":31,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.024839999999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":28817,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30132,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9144834999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2d0db8a8-7324-4fa8-b7fa-7ace924f70ce"}
